Repair only the supplied scientific or grammatical issues. Return {sections:[{id:number,patches:[{before:string,after:string,issueIndex:number}],reason:string}]}. Include each supplied section exactly once. Use exact unique substrings in its candidate. At most 3 non-overlapping patches per section; their combined BEFORE text must cover at most 35% of that section. issueIndex refers to that section's issues. Keep wording elsewhere unchanged. Restore the original meaning, uncertainty and proposal status. No extra style pass. If bounded repairs cannot solve the issues, return patches:[] and explain.
INPUT DATA:
{"sections": [{"id": 4, "heading": "Planned Evaluation", "original": "We plan to report forecast errors for every evaluation day and to inspect unusually hot days separately. Difficult days will remain in the overall result [S2]. The report will also state which forecasts lacked an eligible weather observation. This makes a missing-input failure distinguishable from a model error on a fully observed input, without discarding either from the record.", "candidate": "We plan to report forecast errors for each evaluation day and separately inspect unusually hot days. Difficult days will remain in the overall results. The report will also state which forecasts lacked an eligible weather observation, making a missing-input failure distinguishable from a model error on fully observed inputs without discarding either from the record.", "issues": [{"originalQuote": "Difficult days will remain in the overall result [S2].", "revisedQuote": "Difficult days will remain in the overall results.", "problem": "The revision removes the citation to S2, losing explicit attribution for the requirement to include difficult days in the overall results."}]}], "sources": [{"id": "S1", "title": "Controlled source packet: domain and evidence brief", "excerpt": "The forecasting study predicts next-day electricity demand for one campus building. Weather observations recorded after the forecast deadline are unavailable inputs. Occupancy is represented by a published timetable rather than personal tracking. The study does not estimate household electricity use.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}, {"id": "S2", "title": "Controlled source packet: experimental design brief", "excerpt": "The evaluation will cover 42 consecutive days. A seasonal baseline and a learned forecaster will use the same information cutoff. The final 14 days will be held out from fitting. Forecast errors will be reported for all days, including unusually hot days.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}]}
